    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XVIII.—पिठरजकपाल = a fragment produced from (i. e. of)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "a jar. Râmarshi says कपालं अर्पितं गले यस्य which is unauthorised.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "The usual method gives quite good enough sense—“whose neck",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "is tied to a fragment of a pot.”—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XIX.—Although the worldly enjoyments available are so",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "poor, still the love of them is not destroyed. This Stanza occurs at",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "p. 304 of the Kâvyasangraha.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "St. XX.—कविजनानां श्रेष्ठकवीनां विशेषैर्विशेषवचनैः says Râmarshi, which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "is not correct. गुरुकृतम् = made much of. The first two compari-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "sons are common. Comp. Das'arupâvaloka p. 193.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXI.—दाहात्म्यम् seems a more appropriate reading here.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "माहात्म्यम् would mean simply greatness. On पततु Râmarshi says लिङर्थे",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "लोट् पतेदिति संभावना ॥ जटिल = उद्बुद्ध. कामान् = विषयान् (Râmarshi.) Comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन शाम्यति. This Stanza also occurs at p. 302",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXII.—फल is better than बिस as more commonly used in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "such places. See St. 93 for one instance. अनुमन्तुम् = अङ्गीकर्तुं सोढुम्.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "(Râmarshi.) Comp. Miscellaneous St. 28.—Mâlinî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXIII.—तृणं यथा = the more common expression would be तृ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "णमिव. This Stanza occurs at p. 308 of the Kâvyasangraha.—Hâriṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r9",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXIV.—उपासित &c. is a Dvandva compound the first mem-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ber stopping at गुरु. मानद = महत् (Râmarshi.) The other commenta-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tor derives it from दो अवखण्डने; rightly, but wrongly analyses it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "thus मानं ददाति. एकान्ततः = immutably, decidedly.—S'ârdûlavikrîdita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r10",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXV.—नृपशतैर्यातम्—comp. Stanza 5 इव—see St. 32 Nîti-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "s'ataka. लेशे is somewhat remarkable though justifiable see Siddh.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Kaum. I., 311 and note there by Prof. Târânâth. विषाद i. e. for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "having so little. प्रत्युत = on the contrary.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r11",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXVI.—The readings with भ्रंश yield a meaning of more",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "force than the others. नन्वणुः = but insignificantly small. The",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
